# "Sacrifice a nontoken artifact": the Thopter tokens it makes are artifacts but tokens, so they are never offered (CR 111.1).
# On turn 1 and 3 Bot1 sacrifices Mox Jet then Mox Sapphire, chosen among the Moxen and the Foundry. On turn 5 the only
# nontoken artifact left is the Foundry itself, with two Thopter tokens beside it: a Thopter is refused as a sacrifice (the
# choice offers the Foundry alone) and the Foundry is sacrificed as its own cost; the ability still resolves for a third
# Thopter and 1 more life (CR 602.2b, 113.7a).

